{
  "id": "kitchen-vs1",
  "title": "Grandma's Kitchen",
  "story_for_agents": "Grandma has moved out; her sunny kitchen is half packed. You and her ginger cat recover the memory of baking together. The fridge door is covered in your crayon drawings and a photo of you as a toddler, a big apron and a tiny one hang by the back door, a step stool with floury handprints stands at the counter, and the height marks on the door casing have little crayon stars. The cat sleeps in a packing box on the cookie cutters until milk wakes it. You roll the dough, cut stars, bake them on the sun mark the picture recipe shows, and put the cookies on grandma's plate: the recipe card on the wall turns round by itself into the photo of the two of you baking (the memory). The cat leaps for the cookies, knocks the flour sack off the dresser and bursts it in the sunbeam, then leaves white paw prints to the dark gap under the fridge, where it has hidden its toys and the back-door key (the empty hook on the key board has ginger fur on it). The rolling pin sweeps the key out and the back door opens onto the garden and the greenhouse. No words: the room, the cat, the light and the sounds tell it.",
  "coords": "Blender metres, Z up: +Y north (back door wall), -Y south (range and baking counter), +X east (window and sink), -X west (dresser and table). Camera at (0, 0, 1.30). A mesh belongs to the first visible object that lists it, so the pickups come first; fx.js moves ownership when a prop changes place (tray into the oven, cat to the dresser and the fridge). Zones are invisible tap boxes for small or flat things (the dial's control strip, the gap under the fridge, the height marks).",
  "camera": { "eye": [0, 0, 1.3], "startYaw": 0, "startPitch": -6, "fov": 78, "back": 0.55 },
  "hints": 3,
  "intro": [{ "fx": "intro" }],
  "pickNodes": { "cutterPick": "cutter", "pinPick": "rolling_pin" },
  "focusFirst": ["milkPour", "pinRoll", "cutStars", "ovenIn", "gapSweep"],
  "memoryFlag": "memory",
  "coach": { "target": "door", "icon": "key" },
  "items": {
    "milk": {},
